WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.300
- The app store is the world's

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.638
largest app marketplace.

00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:07.090
(applause)

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.280
- Carplay will also support

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.077
third-party navigation apps.

00:00:10.077 --> 00:00:11.826
(applause)

00:00:11.826 --> 00:00:13.993
(running)

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.940
- Oh hey, we made it.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:18.773
- [Joanna Stern] All right, all right.

00:00:18.773 --> 00:00:19.690
You get the point.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.490
Apple's annual developers conference

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.450
was a little bit different this year.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:26.040
And by different I mean
there was no live audience

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.340
and it was streamed.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.300
Yes, my dog was finally able to attend.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.000
What wasn't different?

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.150
Two hours of new software features

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.743
for your iPhone, iPad, Watch and Mac.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.310
I've rounded up the biggest announcements

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.650
by operating system, marking what I think

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:44.120
are the most exciting features,

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.070
and added some crowd responses.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.355
For old time's sake.

00:00:47.355 --> 00:00:48.700
(crowd cheers)

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.859
And also marking the most "meh" features.

00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:52.692
(crickets croak)

00:00:52.692 --> 00:00:53.942
Yes, denoted by crickets.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.070
First up, IOS fourteen.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.140
The biggest change?

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.980
You can now decorate and
organize your home screen.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.120
There's new feature called App Library,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.350
which will group your
apps into categories.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.470
So you don't have to make your own folders

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.150
or flip through pages and pages of icons.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.280
Your main home screen
can now be customized

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.083
with widgets too, like
weather or your calender.

00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:18.710
(lady claps softly)

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.330
I'm also excited about
the new messages features.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.107
You can now pin your most important chains

00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:25.789
and you can reply to
specific messages inline.

00:01:25.789 --> 00:01:28.400
(crowd cheers)

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.187
Also great, a new translation tool.

00:01:30.187 --> 00:01:32.108
- [Female Speaking To Phone]
What are your store hours?

00:01:32.108 --> 00:01:34.360
- [Phone] (Spanish translation)

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.270
- [Joanna Stern] The mass stuff,

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.040
well Siri no longer takes up

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.220
the whole screen.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.970
Sure that's great, but its not useful

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:41.730
if the assistant isn't any smarter.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:42.563
(beeping)

00:01:42.563 --> 00:01:44.510
- [Siri] Sorry, I didn't quite get that.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:45.520
- [Joanna Stern] And
then there are more ways

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.370
to customize your Memojis.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.830
Including with a mask, because,

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.610
well because.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.240
I have to say I was super excited

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.170
about all the WatchOS7
features we heard about today,

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.480
though I was left expecting some more too.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.770
Yes its finally getting sleep tracking.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.320
Like other wearables it will show you

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.630
your periods of sleep
and when you wake up.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:07.330
And if you're worried about battery life,

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.800
well it will remind you to charge

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.890
when you wake up.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.610
- [Male Presenter] Apple
watch is the first watch

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.910
to deliver automatic detection.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.360
When you start washing your hands,

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.420
it's sensing how long you actually wash.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.170
- [Joanna Stern] Yeah this
is pretty great because

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.950
counting yourself during hand washing,

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.470
is hard.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.528
I can't say I'm psyched about this.

00:02:25.528 --> 00:02:28.278
(crickets croak)

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:31.570
Plus with the global pandemic going on,

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.610
I was expecting to hear more
about some health features.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.370
Perhaps that will come with the
next Watch hardware release.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.610
iPadOS didn't get as many
features as in years past,

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.270
but Apple did fix some long time problems.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.750
An incoming call will no longer

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.510
take over the whole screen.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.620
You can also search from anywhere.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.330
The Apple Pencil unlocks a whole bunch

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.460
of new handwriting features, so instead

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.820
of having to switch
between typing and writing,

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.440
you can now use the scribble feature

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.260
to write into search fields and more.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.800
Yes things seem to be
more easily accessible,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.790
but getting around is
still confusing in iPadOS.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.700
Also, where is the multi user support

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.260
for the iPad, Apple?

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.820
Parents have wanted this for years,

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.750
and not on the Apple TV.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.720
And lastly there is a lot of buzz around

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.610
the next version of MacOS, called Big Sur.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.860
The operating system is getting

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.486
a full visual overhaul.

00:03:19.486 --> 00:03:21.490
The biggest news is that Apple's moving

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.240
its Macs from Intel processors

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.340
to its own Apple Silicon.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.664
Why are they doing this?

00:03:26.664 --> 00:03:28.480
- When we make bold changes,

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.038
it's for one simple yet powerful reason.

00:03:31.038 --> 00:03:33.720
So we can make much better products.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:34.970
- [Joanna Stern] Well, specifically

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.510
it should make battery life better,

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.210
and yes there will be other
major performance improvements.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.910
And the ability to run
iPhone and iPad apps natively

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:42.940
on the Mac.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.630
Apple is working with app makers now

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.900
to start the transition, and it will ship

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.680
the first Mac later this
year with the new chips.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.180
But Tim Cook also said there would be

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.280
more Intel Macs coming soon.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.888
My reaction to this is both a little

00:03:54.888 --> 00:03:56.160
(crowd cheers)

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.195
and a little

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:58.690
(crickets croak)

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.760
All in all, it was a
pretty packed keynote,

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.770
without me having to
go to a packed theater

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.900
to hear the news, and listen to a lot of

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.730
superfluous clapping.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.160
I'm not sure why we haven't been attending

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.393
Apple events this way for years.

